## Authentication Patterns

### Pattern 1: Explicit Credentials (Recommended)

```elixir
# Pass credentials on every authenticated call
{:ok, balances} = Spot.get_balances(%{}, [
  auth_credentials: %{
    api_key: "your_api_key",
    api_secret: "your_api_secret",
    testnet: true
  }
])
```

### Pattern 2: Multi-Account Management

```elixir
# Different credentials for different accounts
accounts = [
  %{api_key: "account1_key", api_secret: "account1_secret"},
  %{api_key: "account2_key", api_secret: "account2_secret"}
]

Enum.map(accounts, fn creds ->
  Spot.get_balances(%{}, [auth_credentials: creds])
end)
```

### Pattern 3: Credential Rotation

```elixir
# Retry with fresh credentials on auth errors
case Spot.place_order(params, [auth_credentials: creds]) do
  {:ok, order} -> {:ok, order}
  {:error, :unauthorized} ->
    # Get fresh credentials and retry
    new_creds = get_fresh_credentials()
    Spot.place_order(params, [auth_credentials: new_creds])
  error -> error
end
```

