## Environment Variables (For Your Code, Not Library)

**The library never reads these.** Your test code or IEx helpers can read them:

```bash
# Testnet credentials (read by YOUR code, not library)
export BINANCE_TESTNET_API_KEY="your_testnet_key"
export BINANCE_TESTNET_API_SECRET="your_testnet_secret"
export BYBIT_TESTNET_API_KEY="your_testnet_key"
export BYBIT_TESTNET_API_SECRET="your_testnet_secret"
```

Then in your code:

```elixir
# YOUR code reads ENV and passes to library
api_key = System.get_env("BINANCE_TESTNET_API_KEY")
api_secret = System.get_env("BINANCE_TESTNET_API_SECRET")

Spot.get_balances(%{}, [
  auth_credentials: %{
    api_key: api_key,
    api_secret: api_secret,
    testnet: true
  }
])
```

